## 5. `transit/config/stops`

Ordered list of the stops the publisher is serving. Republished on change and at publisher startup.

### Schema

| Key | Type | Required | Meaning |
|---|---|---|---|
| `v` | int | yes | contract version |
| `stops` | array | yes | ordered; array order **is** the button cycle order |

Each element:

| Key | Type | Required | Meaning |
|---|---|---|---|
| `id` | string | yes | stop ID; matches a `transit/departures/<id>` topic |
| `label` | string | yes | display name, UTF-8, capped at 20 characters |

### Example

```json
{
  "v": 1,
  "stops": [
    {"id": "60500445", "label": "Hauptplatz"},
    {"id": "60500446", "label": "Taubenmarkt"},
    {"id": "60501234", "label": "Rudolfstraße"}
  ]
}
```

Adding or removing a stop is a publisher-side configuration change. It is **never** a reflash.

The display caches departures for every stop it has received and switches between them from RAM on button press — no network round trip, no perceptible latency.

